I'm not sure where you're starting from for that rule--it's not in Grep's
original query, and it's not Tolkien (Gandalf the Grey/White definitely used
magic to kill).  The closest that's popping immediately to mind is Final
Fantasy's white mage/white wizard, which is more of a healer, but even they
had access to some nice damage spells (Holy being the best).

This seems almost like saying that a lawful knight can't use his sword to
kill, which is obviously silly.

Grep's point was that magic is generally viewed as either chaotic (you're
magical, and so you can do whatever you want) or lawful (magic requires
discipline, focus, and control; if you botch your ritual/spell up, you're
toast); if anything, neutral seems more of a stretch, though it's hard to
argue against.



